<title>GERMANY: Gaddum - EMU outs must not get access to ECB loans.</title>
<headline>Gaddum - EMU outs must not get access to ECB loans.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank Deputy President Johann Wilhelm Gaddum said on Wednesday said that non-members of the planned single European currency should not be given access to credit facilities of the European central bank (ECB).</p>
<p>Giving non-members such access ran counter to the sovereignty of a currency region, he said in the text of a speech, due to be given at a conference in Bonn.</p>
<p>&quot;Nowhere in the world do non-members of a currency region have a right to take part in the money creation process of a foreign currency region,&quot; Gaddum said.</p>
<p>Gaddum said the argument to give non-EMU members access to European central bank funds had arisen in discussions surrounding the planned &quot;Target&quot; system for interbank payments.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
